BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ummi-20260407@ummi.local
DTSTAMP:20260926T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260407
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260408
SUMMARY:Your prenatal vitamins
DESCRIPTION:Folic acid\, 400 micrograms a day until 12 weeks. Choose a preg
 nancy multivitamin: ordinary ones and cod liver oil can contain vitamin A 
 (retinol)\, which is not safe in pregnancy. NHS.\n\nAlso today:\n• Adhā
 n and iqāmah before every prayer (With your hand on your stomach. From Ma
 rriage to Parenthood\, p.110.)\n• Sūrah al-Qadr (97) over two dates (Re
 cite once\, blow on the dates\, eat them on an empty stomach. From Marriag
 e to Parenthood\, p.110.)\n• A sweet apple in the morning (Apple on an e
 mpty stomach is praised in Makārim al-Akhlāq\, p.173. From Marriage to P
 arenthood\, p.109.)\n• A tiny amount of Khāke Shifāʾ before sunset (N
 o bigger than a lentil\, with the intention of shifāʾ. Sistani allows ea
 ting the turbah of Imām Ḥusayn (as) only up to a chickpea’s size\, fo
 r healing (Islamic Laws\, ruling 2645). Soil can carry toxoplasmosis (NHS)
 \, so tell your midwife you take it. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.110.)
 \n• Vitamin D\, 10 micrograms a day (The NHS advises a 10 microgram supp
 lement every day from October to March\, and all year if you usually cover
  most of your skin outdoors. UK milk is not usually fortified\, so food al
 one will not cover it.)\n\nWeek 4\, month 1 of the guide.
CATEGORIES:Wellness
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
