 tomach. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.110.)\n• A sweet apple in the mo
 rning (Apple on an empty stomach is praised in Makārim al-Akhlāq\, p.173
 . From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.109.)\n• A tiny amount of Khāke Shif
 āʾ before sunset (No bigger than a lentil\, with the intention of shifā
 ʾ. Sistani allows eating the turbah of Imām Ḥusayn (as) only up to a c
 hickpea’s size\, for healing (Islamic Laws\, ruling 2645). Soil can carr
 y toxoplasmosis (NHS)\, so tell your midwife you take it. From Marriage to
  Parenthood\, p.110.)\n• Your prenatal vitamins (Folic acid\, 400 microg
 rams a day until 12 weeks. Choose a pregnancy multivitamin: ordinary ones 
