SUMMARY:A pomegranate before breakfast
DESCRIPTION:On an empty stomach. Imām al-Kāẓim (as): a pomegranate eate
 n on Friday before food lights the heart for forty mornings. al-Kāfī\, V
 ol. 6\, p.355.\n\nAlso today:\n• Adhān and iqāmah before every prayer 
 (With your hand on your stomach. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.110.)\n
 • Sūrah Yāsīn (36) and Sūrah aṣ-Ṣāffāt (37) (Then blow gently 
 on your stomach. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.109.)\n• Sūrah al-Qadr
  (97) over two dates (Recite once\, blow on the dates\, eat them on an emp
 ty stomach. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.110.)\n• A sweet apple in th
 e morning (Apple on an empty stomach is praised in Makārim al-Akhlāq\, p
 .173. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.109.)\n• A tiny amount of Khāke S
 hifāʾ before sunset (No bigger than a lentil\, with the intention of shi
 fāʾ. Sistani allows eating the turbah of Imām Ḥusayn (as) only up to 
 a chickpea’s size\, for healing (Islamic Laws\, ruling 2645). Soil can c
 arry toxoplasmosis (NHS)\, so tell your midwife you take it. From Marriage
  to Parenthood\, p.110.)\n• Your prenatal vitamins (Folic acid\, 400 mic
 rograms a day until 12 weeks. Choose a pregnancy multivitamin: ordinary on
 es and cod liver oil can contain vitamin A (retinol)\, which is not safe i
 n pregnancy. NHS.)\n• Vitamin D\, 10 micrograms a day (The NHS advises a
  10 microgram supplement every day from October to March\, and all year if
  you usually cover most of your skin outdoors. UK milk is not usually fort
 ified\, so food alone will not cover it.)\n\nWeek 4\, month 1 of the guide
 .
CATEGORIES:Food
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
