BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ummi-20260609@ummi.local
DTSTAMP:20260926T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260609
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260610
SUMMARY:Istighfār 7 times
DESCRIPTION:Astaghfirullāha Rabbī wa atūbu ilayh. From Marriage to Paren
 thood\, p.112.\n\nAlso today:\n• Sūrah al-Furqān 25:74 (The prayer for
  comfort in your family. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.112.)\n• Ṣala
 wāt 140 times after each prayer (From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.112.)\n
 • Ṣalātul Layl (As much as you can manage. Sistani allows it any time
  after ʿIshāʾ until Fajr (Islamic Laws\, ruling 760)\; if you miss it\,
  make it up later. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.113.)\n• Sūrah al-Qa
 dr (97) in one rakʿah of every prayer (After al-Fātiḥah\, in the first
  or second rakʿah. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.112.)\n• After the d
 aily prayers: al-Kawthar\, al-Qadr\, long ṣalawāt (Sūrah al-Kawthar (1
 08)\, Sūrah al-Qadr (97)\, then the long ṣalawāt with your hand on you
 r stomach. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.112.)\n• Sūrah at-Tīn (95) 
 over two figs (Eat them on an empty stomach. From Marriage to Parenthood\,
  p.113.)\n• Sweet apples\, honey and pomegranates (Sweet pomegranate “
 improves the child”: al-Kāfī\, Vol. 6\, p.355. From Marriage to Parent
 hood\, p.112.)\n• Nutrient-rich foods (Lentils and beans\, wholegrains\,
  cheese and yoghurt\, and leafy greens (NHS).)\n\nWeek 13\, month 4 of the
  guide.
CATEGORIES:Recitation
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
