SUMMARY:Sūrah al-Qadr (97) in one rakʿah of every prayer
DESCRIPTION:After al-Fātiḥah\, in the first or second rakʿah. From Marr
 iage to Parenthood\, p.112.\n\nAlso today:\n• Sūrah al-Furqān 25:74 (T
 he prayer for comfort in your family. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.112.
 )\n• Istighfār 7 times (Astaghfirullāha Rabbī wa atūbu ilayh. From M
 arriage to Parenthood\, p.112.)\n• Ṣalawāt 140 times after each praye
 r (From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.112.)\n• Ṣalātul Layl (As much as 
 you can manage. Sistani allows it any time after ʿIshāʾ until Fajr (Isl
 amic Laws\, ruling 760)\; if you miss it\, make it up later. From Marriage
  to Parenthood\, p.113.)\n• After the daily prayers: al-Kawthar\, al-Qad
 r\, long ṣalawāt (Sūrah al-Kawthar (108)\, Sūrah al-Qadr (97)\, then 
 the long ṣalawāt with your hand on your stomach. From Marriage to Paren
 thood\, p.112.)\n• Sūrah at-Tīn (95) over two figs (Eat them on an emp
 ty stomach. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.113.)\n• Sweet apples\, hone
 y and pomegranates (Sweet pomegranate “improves the child”: al-Kāfī\
 , Vol. 6\, p.355. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.112.)\n• Nutrient-rich
  foods (Lentils and beans\, wholegrains\, cheese and yoghurt\, and leafy g
 reens (NHS).)\n\nWeek 16\, month 4 of the guide.
CATEGORIES:Sūrah
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
