BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ummi-20260901@ummi.local
DTSTAMP:20260926T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260901
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260902
SUMMARY:Iron-rich foods
DESCRIPTION:Red meat\, beans and chickpeas\, nuts\, dried apricots and fort
 ified cereals. Your iron is checked at booking and at 28 weeks\, and you
 ’ll be offered a supplement if it is low (NHS).\n\nAlso today:\n• Ṣa
 lawāt 140 times (From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• Sūrah al-An
 ʿām (6) over almonds after Fajr (For forty days\, then eat the almonds. 
 From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• Sūrah an-Nūr (24) (Often\, fr
 om this month onward. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• The five 
 sūrahs after your prayers (After the daily prayers and the tasbīḥ of S
 ayyidah Fāṭimah (as): al-Ḥadīd (57)\, al-Ḥashr (59)\, aṣ-Ṣaff 
 (61)\, al-Jumuʿah (62) and at-Taghābun (64). From Marriage to Parenthood
 \, p.114.)\n• Sūrah al-Qadr (97) and al-Ikhlāṣ (112) in the daily pr
 ayers (After al-Fātiḥah. Once you start al-Ikhlāṣ\, finish it rather
  than switching (Sistani\, Islamic Laws\, ruling 974). From Marriage to Pa
 renthood\, p.114.)\n• Sūrah Yāsīn (36) over a quince (Then eat it on 
 an empty stomach. Quince for pregnant women: al-Kāfī\, Vol. 6\, p.22. Fr
 om Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• Melon after your food (After food
  rather than on an empty stomach (Imām al-ʿAskarī (as)\, Mustadrak al-W
 asāʾil\, Vol. 16\, p.410). The pregnancy hadith\, in Mustadrak Vol. 15\,
  p.214\, comes from a Sunni medical collection\, so it is weak. Avoid wate
 r with it.)\n\nWeek 25\, month 7 of the guide.
CATEGORIES:Food
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
BEGIN:VEVENT
UID:ummi-20260902@ummi.local
DTSTAMP:20260926T000000Z
DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260902
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260903
SUMMARY:Ṣalawāt 140 times
DESCRIPTION:From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.\n\nAlso today:\n• Sūrah
  al-Anʿām (6) over almonds after Fajr (For forty days\, then eat the alm
 onds. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• Sūrah an-Nūr (24) (Ofte
 n\, from this month onward. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• The
  five sūrahs after your prayers (After the daily prayers and the tasbī
 ḥ of Sayyidah Fāṭimah (as): al-Ḥadīd (57)\, al-Ḥashr (59)\, aṣ
 -Ṣaff (61)\, al-Jumuʿah (62) and at-Taghābun (64). From Marriage to Pa
 renthood\, p.114.)\n• Sūrah al-Qadr (97) and al-Ikhlāṣ (112) in the 
 daily prayers (After al-Fātiḥah. Once you start al-Ikhlāṣ\, finish i
 t rather than switching (Sistani\, Islamic Laws\, ruling 974). From Marria
 ge to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• Sūrah Yāsīn (36) over a quince (Then ea
 t it on an empty stomach. Quince for pregnant women: al-Kāfī\, Vol. 6\, 
 p.22. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• Melon after your food (Af
 ter food rather than on an empty stomach (Imām al-ʿAskarī (as)\, Mustad
 rak al-Wasāʾil\, Vol. 16\, p.410). The pregnancy hadith\, in Mustadrak V
 ol. 15\, p.214\, comes from a Sunni medical collection\, so it is weak. Av
 oid water with it.)\n• Iron-rich foods (Red meat\, beans and chickpeas\,
  nuts\, dried apricots and fortified cereals. Your iron is checked at book
 ing and at 28 weeks\, and you’ll be offered a supplement if it is low (N
 HS).)\n\nWeek 25\, month 7 of the guide.
CATEGORIES:Recitation
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
