DTSTART;VALUE=DATE:20260919
DTEND;VALUE=DATE:20260920
SUMMARY:Sūrah al-Anʿām (6) over almonds after Fajr
DESCRIPTION:For forty days\, then eat the almonds. From Marriage to Parenth
 ood\, p.114.\n\nAlso today:\n• Ṣalawāt 140 times (From Marriage to Pa
 renthood\, p.114.)\n• Sūrah an-Nūr (24) (Often\, from this month onwar
 d. From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• The five sūrahs after your 
 prayers (After the daily prayers and the tasbīḥ of Sayyidah Fāṭimah 
 (as): al-Ḥadīd (57)\, al-Ḥashr (59)\, aṣ-Ṣaff (61)\, al-Jumuʿah 
 (62) and at-Taghābun (64). From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\n• Sū
 rah al-Qadr (97) and al-Ikhlāṣ (112) in the daily prayers (After al-Fā
 tiḥah. Once you start al-Ikhlāṣ\, finish it rather than switching (Si
 stani\, Islamic Laws\, ruling 974). From Marriage to Parenthood\, p.114.)\
 n• Sūrah Yāsīn (36) over a quince (Then eat it on an empty stomach. Q
 uince for pregnant women: al-Kāfī\, Vol. 6\, p.22. From Marriage to Pare
 nthood\, p.114.)\n• Melon after your food (After food rather than on an 
 empty stomach (Imām al-ʿAskarī (as)\, Mustadrak al-Wasāʾil\, Vol. 16\
 , p.410). The pregnancy hadith\, in Mustadrak Vol. 15\, p.214\, comes from
  a Sunni medical collection\, so it is weak. Avoid water with it.)\n• Ir
 on-rich foods (Red meat\, beans and chickpeas\, nuts\, dried apricots and 
 fortified cereals. Your iron is checked at booking and at 28 weeks\, and y
 ou’ll be offered a supplement if it is low (NHS).)\n\nWeek 27\, month 7 
 of the guide.
CATEGORIES:Sūrah
TRANSP:TRANSPARENT
END:VEVENT
